\viewkind4\uc1 \f1\fs20\b STUDY SHEET\b0\par
\f1\fs32\b In your mouth, in your heart, in your hands\b0\fs24\par
\f1\fs20 Torah: Deuteronomy 29:10\u8211?31:30 | Haftarah: Isaiah 61:10\u8211?63:9 | Gospel: John 12:41\u8211?50\par
\f0\fs22\i In Nitzavim/Vayelech the word is not in heaven but very near \u8212? in your mouth, in your heart, in your hands, to d\u243? it; God first circumcises the heart (30:6), and what you received you pass on, from Moses to Joshua, from generation to generation.\i0\par
\par\f0\fs24 
\par\b\fs28 \u167?0. Observation round\b0\fs24\par


\par\b\fs24 0.1 Blind observation\b0\fs24\par


\par The text is full of verbs of st\u233?pping in, ch\u243?osing, d\u243?ing, p\u225?ssing on. You all stand present today to enter \u237?nto the covenant (29:10-12), \u225?lso on behalf of the one not yet here (29:14). There is a hidden figure: the root that bears \u8216?gall and wormwood\u8217?, the person who secretly bl\u233?sses himself and yet walks his own way (29:17-18). After exile you ret\u250?rn and d\u243? (30:1-2). The commandment is not too heavy, not far, not in heaven \u8212? \u8216?very n\u237?gh unto thee, in thy mouth and in thy heart, that thou mayest d\u243? it\u8217? (30:11-14). \u8216?Ch\u243?ose life\u8217? (30:19). And Vayelech: be strong, h\u225?nd it over to Joshua (31:7); read this Torah aloud every seven years \u8212? men, women, children, stranger \u8212? that they hear, learn and d\u243? (31:11-12); the Torah and the song as witness (31:19,26).\par


\par\b\fs24 0.2 The four axes as an open question\b0\fs24\par


\par Where does the weight fall \u8212? on what God gives (Source), on what the human answers (Will), on the wholeness between hidden and open (Coherence), or on the movement through time (Trajectory)? I leave that open here and read it off only after the blocks.\par


\par\b\fs24 0.3 Read-off center of gravity\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? The rhetorical mass of the parashah (30:11-20 + all of Vayelech) lies on doing, choosing, handing on \u8212? not on receiving. The hinge with l\u225?st week makes it sharp: Ki Tavo ended on 29:4 (\u8216?the LORD hath not given you an heart to perceive\u8217?), Nitzavim arrives at 30:14 (the word is alr\u233?ady in your heart, to do). The same two verses, side by side, opposite emphasis. Th\u225?t is the turn: from the withheld heart to the acting heart.\par


\par\b\fs24 0.4 Framing test\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8908? The reflex puts the weight on receiving / defencelessness, and there is one verse that truly carries that reading: 30:6, \u8216?the LORD will circumcise thine heart to love Him.\u8217? \u-10179?\u-8222? That verse is no subclause \u8212? it is the gr\u243?und. B\u250?t the parashah does not set it as climax; it sets it as pr\u233?condition: because the heart is freed and the word is br\u243?ught near, d\u243?ing is no longer an autonomous feat but a reachable answer. So the test does not pull \u8216?grace\u8217? and \u8216?doing\u8217? apart \u8212? it grounds the doing \u237?n the given nearness. Whoever makes 30:6 the landing place and 30:11-20 a subclause imposes the template; the text turns it around. The tension 30:6 \u8596?\u-498? 30:14 remains an open anomaly, not smoothed over.\par


\par\b\fs28 \u167?1. The thread\b0\fs24\par


\par The word is not far away and not in heaven \u8212? it is brought near, in your mouth and your heart, to d\u243? it; and that done faithfulness is not private but p\u225?ssed on: from \u250?s to our children, from Moses to Joshua, from this generation to the next. The grace is that it has been made reachable; the calling is that you step in, choose and pass it on.\par


\par\b\fs28 \u167?2. Peshat per block\b0\fs24\par


\par\b\fs24 29:10-14\b0\fs24\par


\par All stand present, from head to water-drawer, to enter \u237?nto the covenant and its oath; God confirms them as a people \u8212? \u225?lso with the one \u8216?not here today\u8217?. \u-10179?\u-8222? Key: stepping in (actively entering), and the covenant reaching beyond the present generation.\par


\par\b\fs24 29:15-28\b0\fs24\par


\par Warning: the root bearing poison is the person who secretly bl\u233?sses himself (29:18). Wrath, exile. Then 29:29 (MT 29:28): \u8216?the secret things belong to the LORD; the revealed to \u250?s and our children, to d\u243? them.\u8217? \u-10179?\u-8222? Contrast hidden \u8596?\u-498? revealed; the revealed side is explicitly a d\u243?-command.\par


\par\b\fs24 30:1-10\b0\fs24\par


\par After exile: return (teshuvah), God gathers, God circumcises the heart (30:6). \u-10179?\u-8222? Here is the Source pole: the restoration is God\u8217?s act, and the freed heart precedes the loving.\par


\par\b\fs24 30:11-14\b0\fs24\par


\par The commandment is not too wondrous, not far, not in heaven, not over the sea \u8212? near, in mouth and heart, \u8216?to do it\u8217?. Three times la\u8217?asoto (to do it). \u-10179?\u-8223? Textual witness: 4QDeut-b/LXX add \u8216?and in your hands\u8217? \u8212? variant, strengthens the doing-side.\par


\par\b\fs24 30:15-20\b0\fs24\par


\par \u8216?I have set before you life and good, death and evil\u8230? ch\u243?ose life.\u8217? \u-10179?\u-8222? The choice is laid with the human; heaven and earth as witnesses.\par


\par\b\fs24 31:1-30 (Vayelech)\b0\fs24\par


\par Moses (120) hands over to Joshua (\u8216?be strong and of good courage\u8217?, 31:7); the Torah is written and read aloud every seven years to the wh\u243?le people incl. children and stranger (31:11-12); the foretold falling away; the song and the Torah bes\u237?de the ark, as witness (31:19,26). \u-10179?\u-8222? Handover and transmission as a movement of its own.\par


\par\b\fs28 \u167?3. The two bearing axes\b0\fs24\par


\par\b\fs24 Will (bearing)\b0\fs24\par


\par Stepping in (29:11), returning and doing (30:2), the near doing (30:11-14), choosing (30:19), being strong and handing over (31:7), hearing-learning-doing (31:12). Answer within reach, not self-sufficiency: the word is brought t\u243? you. Open anomaly: where does \u8216?chosen doing\u8217? turn into \u8216?my own strength\u8217?? (cf. 8:17)\par


\par\b\fs24 Coherence (bearing, second pole)\b0\fs24\par


\par No gap between the hidden heart and the public deed: the root of poison lies in the secret self-blessing (29:18); the revealed side is \u243?urs to do (29:29); and the people stand surety as one body \u8212? arvut. The song as witness (31:19) guards precisely the coherence between promise and future deed. Open anomaly: the nekudot on \u8216?for us and our children\u8217? \u8212? tradition set a mark on exactly this passed-on responsibility; why?\par


\par\b\fs24 Source and Trajectory (supporting)\b0\fs24\par


\par Source is real (30:3-6) but does not carry the weight here; Trajectory (exile\u8594?return, Moses\u8594?Joshua, generation\u8594?generation) is r\u237?sing and feeds the \u8216?passing on\u8217? side, but serves Will, not as a core of its own.\par


\par\b\fs28 \u167?4. Deepening \u8212? the sources round\b0\fs24\par


\par \i Order followed; yield per witness kept brief.\i0 \par


\par \b Van de Giessen \u-10179?\u-8222? \u8212?\b0  (1) nekudot / puncta extraordinaria on lanu ulevaneinu (29:29 / MT 29:28); function probably: marking uncertain letters (Qumran usage). (2) 30:14: 4QDeut-b and LXX read a plus, \u8216?and in your h\u225?nds, to do it\u8217?. Both verses close with a setumah. \u8594? The textual ground strengthens the action-side even before any interpretation.\par


\par \b Onkelos \u8212?\b0  not yet verified; open verification point (Sefaria). \u9898?\par


\par \b Rashi \u-10179?\u-8222? \u8212?\b0  30:12: w\u233?re it in heaven, it would remain your duty to go up after it and learn (reachability = ground for effort). 29:29: hidden = private conduct (not our responsibility), revealed = indeed ours; the dots qualify that collective duty (binding only \u225?fter the Jordan) \u8212? here kol Yisrael arevim hangs.\par


\par \b Ibn Ezra \u-10179?\u-8222? (brake) \u8212?\b0  \u8216?not in heaven\u8217? merely unfolds \u8216?too wondrous\u8217? (v.11): n\u243?t-unreachable, grammatically. Prunes away the over-pious reading.\par


\par \b Ramban \u-10179?\u-8222? (coherence) \u8212?\b0  the near commandment = teshuvah: return is not far, needs no prophet or distant sages, do-able even in exile. Divergence with Rashi (whole Torah vs. return) \u8212? both land on human abil\u237?ty.\par


\par \b Midrash / aggadah \u-10179?\u-8223? \u8212?\b0  lo bashamayim hi: the Torah is handed over to the human; even a Voice from heaven is overruled (oven of Achnai). And on the dots: Ezra honestly holds the uncertainty rather than polishing it away.\par


\par \b Did the round shift the center of gravity?\b0  Yes. From a Source / receiving landing to Will / Coherence: the near word is near to be d\u243?ne and p\u225?ssed on. Every witness pushes the same way; the reflex (30:6 as climax) is exactly what the sources contradict.\par


\par\b\fs28 \u167?5. Directional test as horizon\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? (confessional, no climax) John 12:47-50 puts Yeshua\u8217?s l\u225?st word to the crowd on w\u243?rds that want to be done: \u8216?if any man hear my words, and believe not\u8230?\u8217? (12:47); \u8216?I have not spoken of myself; the Father gave me a commandment what to say\u8217? (12:49-50). The near-word-to-do, embodied \u8212? a Mouth that speaks \u8216?not of Itself\u8217?, precisely the opposite of the secret self-blessing of 29:18. Romans 10:6-8 (Paul cites 30:12-14) is the confessional bridge: the \u8216?word nigh thee\u8217? becomes the word of faith \u8212? horizon, woven, n\u243?t overriding the peshat (the plain sense stays: the commandment, to do it). \u-10179?\u-8908? 12:48 (\u8216?the word shall judge\u8217?) is kept sober as the seriousness of the near word, not as a triumph- or judgment-climax.\par


