\par\b\fs28 \u167?7. Podcast translation\b0\fs24\par


\par You know the difference between something on the top shelf \u8212? you have to fetch a ladder, ask someone, reach for it \u8212? and something already in front of you on the countertop. God does not say here: climb to heaven to fetch my word. He says: it lies already in your hand. In your mouth, in your heart, in your hands. W\u233? did not have to go up for it; it was brought t\u243? us. B\u250?t \u8212? mark this \u8212? near is not the same as non-committal. What lies in your hand asks to be d\u243?ne. And not only you: you lay it in your child\u8217?s hand, as Moses laid it in Joshua\u8217?s hand. It is not a burden you carry alone; it is grace that became do-able, and that you pass on.\par


